ct":false,"prior":102.0,"yoy":57.8},{"cur":32.0,"metric":"Operating Profit (Rs cr)","nd":0,"pct":false,"prior":18.0,"yoy":77.8},{"cur":19.6,"metric":"OPM (%)","nd":1,"pct":true,"prior":17.7,"yoy":1.9},{"cur":21.0,"metric":"PAT (Rs cr)","nd":0,"pct":false,"prior":14.0,"yoy":50.0},{"cur":1.43,"metric":"EPS (Rs, annualised)","nd":2,"pct":false,"prior":1.09,"yoy":31.2}]},"year":{"label":"FY26","note":"EPS = exit-quarter annualised (not summed)","prior":"FY25","rows":[{"cur":553,"metric":"Revenue (Rs cr)","nd":0,"pct":false,"prior":309,"yoy":79.0},{"cur":100,"metric":"Operating Profit (Rs cr)","nd":0,"pct":false,"prior":51,"yoy":96.1},{"cur":18.1,"metric":"OPM (%)","nd":1,"pct":true,"prior":16.5,"yoy":1.6},{"cur":72,"metric":"PAT (Rs cr)","nd":0,"pct":false,"prior":null,"yoy":null},{"cur":1.44,"metric":"EPS (Rs, annualised, exit qtr)","nd":2,"pct":false,"prior":1.24,"yoy":16.1}]}},"profile":{"entities":"Vintage Coffee & Beverages Ltd (Standalone/Consolidated)","mgmt":"","subseg":"Spray-dried instant coffee; Agglomerated coffee; Freeze-dried coffee; Private label consumer packs","themes":"Capacity expansion (Spray & Freeze-dried); Mix shift to consumer packs; Export-led growth; Cost-plus pricing model"},"qtr":"Q3FY26","ratios":[{"label":"ROE %","value":"16.6%"},{"label":"ROCE %","value":"14.1%"},{"label":"D/E","value":"0.2x"},{"label":"Int cover","value":"10.8x"},{"label":"Receivable d","value":"88.0"},{"label":"Inventory d","value":"93.5"},{"label":"Payable d","value":"3.4"},{"label":"OPM %","value":"18.0%"}],"s":"VINCOFE","sec":"Specialty Coffee Processing & Export (Instant/Freeze-Dried)","sec2":"Fast Moving Consumer Goods","sections":{"bull_bear":[{"body":"Funding secured via warrants, preference shares, and European debt tie-up for freeze-dried project. Focus on capacity expansion to capture global demand growth (8-10% CAGR for freeze-dried). Working capital management improving with positive operating cash flow in Q3.","src":"concall","title":"Capital allocation"},{"body":"Raw material price volatility (though hedged by cost-plus model); Working capital intensity (inventory days ~60, debtor days ~60-70); Execution risk on new freeze-dried technology ramp-up; Geographic concentration in exports (though diversifying into Korea, Australia, NZ).","src":"concall","title":"Risks & watch-items"},{"body":"Highly confident; Emphasizes 'sold out' status, full capacity utilization, and successful transition to high-margin consumer packs. Clear visibility on growth trajectory.","src":"concall","title":"Management quality / tone"},{"body":"The company is shifting raw material sourcing from 80-85% domestic to 60% domestic / 40% imported (Uganda, Indonesia) by Q2 FY27 to optimize blends and costs. The freeze-dried segment is already 'sold out' globally for the year, indicating extremely tight supply-demand dynamics favoring Vintage's new capacity.","src":"concall","title":"Non-obvious takeaways"}],"business":[{"body":"Current mix: 50-60% Consumer Packs (doy-packs, tins, jars) vs 40-50% Bulk; Target mix: 70% Consumer / 30% Bulk. Product shift from bulk spray-dried to agglomerated/granulated and freeze-dried. Realization per ton increased from INR 202/kg to INR 240/kg driven by mix.","src":"concall","title":"Segment / subsidiary detail"},{"body":"| Challenge | Beneficiary/Loser | Dir | Conviction | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Global freeze-dried coffee demand outstripping supply with 8-10% growth; Vintage's new capacity commands 30-40% premium. | Vintage Coffee & Beverages Ltd | beneficiary | High | Direct beneficiary of own capacity expansion and mix shift; sold-out order book de-risks volume uptake. |","src":"concall","title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers"}],"latest_quarter":[{"body":"EBITDA margin expanded to 19.1% due to higher value-added product mix and operating leverage. Business operates on a cost-plus model with quarterly price resets, insulating margins from raw material (coffee bean) volatility. Fixed costs will spread over larger volume with new capacity, further aiding margins.","src":"concall","title":"Margins & cost dynamics"}],"outlook":[{"body":"Revenue growth: Implied ~70% CAGR over next 2 years via capacity doubling; Margin: Structural improvement via mix shift (target 70% consumer packs) and operating leverage on new capacity; Order inflow: Strong visibility with Q4 sold out and new capacity pre-booked; Capex/commissioning: 4,500 MT spray-dried commissioning March 2026 (INR 45 Cr); 5,500 MT freeze-dried commissioning FY27 (INR 500 Cr total project cost).","src":"concall","title":"Guidance"},{"body":"Q4 FY26 completely sold out; Additional 4,500 MT spray-dried capacity has confirmed quantity commitments from customers; Freeze-dried capacity expected to run at 65-70% utilization in Year 1.","src":"concall","title":"Order book & pipeline"},{"body":"Phase 1: 4,500 MT spray-dried/agglomerated addition (March '26) taking total to 11,000 MT. Phase 2: 5,500 MT freeze-dried plant (FY27) taking total to 16,500 MT. Phase 3: Potential second 5,500 MT freeze-dried line by FY28/29 (MOU with Telangana govt for INR 1,100 Cr total investment). Freeze-dried commands 30-40% price premium over spray-dried.","src":"concall","title":"Growth verticals / optionality"}]},"sources":["Q3FY26 concall summary","structured quarterly financials"],"thesis":"Vintage Coffee delivered a blowout Q3 with 71% revenue growth and 19.1% EBITDA margins driven by a strategic shift to higher-margin consumer packs (now 50-60% of mix) and full utilization of existing capacity. The imminent commissioning of 4,500 MT spray-dried capacity (March '26) and a 5,500 MT freeze-dried plant (FY27) positions the company for a doubling of capacity with significantly higher realizations, supported by a sold-out order book.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":1.27,"fy":"FY22","mcap":2333,"opm":-10.3,"pe":null,"roe":-14.2},{"de":1.13,"fy":"FY2